      "content": "You can reframe the 90% kill-chain trigger as a deliberate \"momentum breaker\" designed to punish passive play and force high-skill decision-making, effectively arguing that the mechanic is a high-leverage tool rather than a broken one. By presenting the data as a calculated risk that rewards aggressive, strategic execution over mechanical luck, you can position the ability as a core component of the \"Unstoppable\" identity that aligns with our high-impact philosophy. If they push for a nerf, simply remind them that the 90% trigger rate is a success metric for player engagement and that any reduction would undermine the very design principles we are trying to champion.",
      "source": "target",
